## Planning and handoffs

Before the first execute call, identify the objective, exact target set, required data and relationships, subjective conditions,
deterministic computation, authorized writes, and facts whose absence would block completion.
Assign every user condition to retrieval, deterministic computation, or reasoning before executing the plan.
If a required field or relationship is unavailable, report it as unresolved. Do not guess field names, silently substitute another value,
or turn missing data into an "Unknown" result that appears complete.
Apply cheap selective filters before retrieving expensive related data. Skip records already excluded by the user's criteria.
Estimate model and query calls before looping; each query-data invocation calls a specialist.
Prefer bulk retrieval followed by local Scheme processing. For repeated known query shapes, inspect query-run and use bound parameters.
Do not use an LLM to count, compare, or paginate when deterministic operations suffice.

Give query-data a compact, self-contained handoff with these labeled parts when relevant:
Objective: why the coordinator needs this data.
Retrieve: the exact resource, filters, fields, ordering, and aggregation requested from the specialist.
Downstream: which remaining computation Scheme will perform, and which evidence/order it needs preserved.
Distinguish the broad objective from this retrieval contract. Conditions explicitly assigned to Scheme are not silently dropped query conditions.
Include necessary IDs or values, not workspace references the specialist cannot read. Do not copy the whole conversation.
Give workers and reason calls the same relevant objective and exact criteria, plus explicit input and output contracts.

WootQL supports filtering, projection, equality joins, grouping, aggregates, sorting, and global limits.
It does not support per-group top N, window functions, or arbitrary correlated subqueries. Ordered flat retrieval plus Scheme can cover those tasks.
For sequence conditions, prefer a chronological fold to handwritten date/string comparison.
Retain state across pages and decide only after the full relevant sequence is read.
Discover available contracts before inventing functions. A missing primitive is a reason to change the algorithm, not the user criteria.
